Stacked on the Sheep Shearer / Romeo & Juliet PR (its `QuestTalkFixture`) and carries the npc and loc op overrides PR's change (`LocOpOverrides`) as a second commit with the same diff; only the last commit is new here.

**Problem.** Doric's Quest was not implemented; Doric's anvils could be used without it.

**Change.** New quest on OpenRune's quest framework. Progress is varp 31 (`doricquest`) through a server-only varbit: 0, 10 started, 100 complete, the values the client and Quest Helper read.
- The opening topics, the start (with a bronze pickaxe), the 6 clay / 4 copper ore / 2 iron ore hand-in (one transaction), and the shortcut when the player already carries them.
- Rewards: 1 QP, 1,300 Mining XP, 180 coins.
- Until the quest is done, Smith on Doric's anvils brings Doric over instead (`LocOpOverrides`).
- The quest start prompt reads "Start Doric's Quest?" for names ending in "Quest" (as in OSRS), "Start the X quest?" otherwise.

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: varbit `doric_quest_progress` 63719.

**Tests.** `DoricsQuestInteractionTest`, plus the quest suites it builds on.

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): RESULTS_PENDING. `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): the dialogue follows the wiki transcript of Doric's Quest. Step values: Quest Helper (BSD).

